From: Ubuntu Embedded Team
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2-ctl: allow libv4l wrapper to validate virtual endpoints

The Rockchip plugin uses role files, which media-info rejects before the
wrapper is called. Keep direct device detection unchanged and retain the
subsequent wrapper open and VIDIOC_QUERYCAP checks.

--- a/utils/v4l2-ctl/v4l2-ctl.cpp
+++ b/utils/v4l2-ctl/v4l2-ctl.cpp
@@ -1338,6 +1338,11 @@
 		break;
 	}
 
+	/* libv4l plugins can expose virtual endpoints backed by regular files.
+	 * In wrapper mode let open/VIDIOC_QUERYCAP validate those endpoints. */
+	if (type == MEDIA_TYPE_UNKNOWN && options[OptUseWrapper])
+		type = MEDIA_TYPE_VIDEO;
+
 	if (type == MEDIA_TYPE_UNKNOWN) {
 		fprintf(stderr, "Unable to detect what device %s is, exiting.\n",
 			device);
